// L4 `H` — `G` with the two `use` lines swapped, and nothing else changed.
//
// ⚠ THE PAIR IS THE INSTRUMENT, NOT EITHER FILE. What is being asked is whether the
// IMPORT ORDER can change what a bare name means, and only two files that differ in
// nothing else can answer it. `G` carries the full three-step history; the short version
// is that these two once compiled DIFFERENT programs (loft#788), then both stopped
// compiling when loft learnt to refuse the ambiguity, and since `L6.2` renamed ours to
// `VoxelChunk` they compile the SAME program — because only one package declares `Chunk`
// now, so there is nothing left for the order to decide.
//
// If these two ever disagree again, the order decides again, and #788 is back.
use hex_world;
use hex_voxel;

fn main() {
  c = Chunk { ck_cx: 1, ck_cz: 2, ck_cells: [] };
  println("PROBE bare literal took THEIRS: {c.ck_cx}");
}
